 "text": "Hi, how are you holding up? The simplest and most effective method is a brightly lit and frequently updated food plot. Bears will usually eat from it all summer until the snow comes. Try keeping it on the opposite side of the camp from your tent. A bear's nose is very powerful, and it can smell food from several hundred yards away. Pick up all the food and keep the bags closed for several days. Then burn the food in a spot out of reach and let the ashes cool before picking them up.",
